{# One control of the bar of either skeleton (issues #447, #448): a button, and what opens under it.

   **No script, like every page of this plane.** What holds the state is a radio button the keyboard
   reaches, its label is the button somebody sees, and the panel is shown while that button is the one
   checked. The three controls share one group, so one of them is open at a time, and the veil of
   _controls.html.twig lies over the page while one is: a click anywhere else closes it, and a second click
   on the button of the one that is open is a click on that veil.

   Two blocks: "trigger", what the button says, and "panel", what opens under it. The caller embeds this
   file and fills them; "control" names the control in the identifiers and the stylesheet, "label" is what
   the button is to whoever does not see it. #}
<div data-control="{{ control }}">
    <input type="radio" name="layout-control" id="layout-control-{{ control }}" aria-label="{{ label }}">
    <label for="layout-control-{{ control }}" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" data-control="trigger">
        {%- block trigger %}{% endblock -%}
    </label>
    <div data-control="panel">
        {%- block panel %}{% endblock -%}
    </div>
</div>
